        <div type="bibliography" xml:space="preserve" xml:lang="en">
            <p>
            <bibl><ptr target="#Vokotopoulou1992"/>, <citedRange>81 no 8, fig. 3b</citedRange></bibl> (<bibl><ptr target="SEG"/> <citedRange>43.325</citedRange></bibl>; <bibl><ptr target="#IDodoneLhôte"/> <citedRange>114</citedRange></bibl>; <bibl><ptr target="#Eidinow2007"/>, <citedRange>74, 76 no 5, 107</citedRange></bibl>); <bibl><ptr target="#IDodoneDVC"/> <citedRange>24A+25A+26B</citedRange></bibl> (<bibl><ptr target="#CIOD"/> <citedRange>24-25</citedRange></bibl> [last consulted 15/07/2026]); <bibl><ptr target="#Dodonaios2019"/>, <citedRange>307 no 73</citedRange></bibl> (G. Giannakis, E.K. Skalisti); <bibl><ptr target="#Johnston2021"/>, <citedRange>114</citedRange></bibl>; <bibl><ptr target="#Giannakis2024a"/>, <citedRange>124</citedRange></bibl>; <bibl><ptr target="#Giannakis2024b"/>, <citedRange>110, 129</citedRange></bibl>.
            </p>
            <p>Cf.    
            <bibl><ptr target="#Dosuna2008"/>, <citedRange>59</citedRange> (on <foreign xml:lang="grc">οἴκησις</foreign>), <citedRange>64</citedRange> (on elision of final nu)</bibl>; <bibl><ptr target="#deJong2015"/>, <citedRange>124</citedRange> (English translation)</bibl>; <bibl><ptr target="Chaniotis2016"/>, <citedRange>§201</citedRange> (classifying inscription on face B as an answer)</bibl>; <bibl><ptr target="#Parker2016"/>, <citedRange>88-89 n. 84</citedRange></bibl>; <bibl><ptr target="#Chaniotis2017a"/>, <citedRange>58</citedRange></bibl>; <bibl><ptr target="#Rizzo2017"/>, <citedRange>730</citedRange> (on consulations about Italy XXX)</bibl>; <bibl><ptr target="#Vecchio2017"/>, <citedRange>110</citedRange> (Italian translation)</bibl>; <bibl><ptr target="#Nocita2018"/>, <citedRange>XXX</citedRange></bibl>; <bibl><ptr target="#GiannakisCrespo2019"/>, <citedRange>50</citedRange></bibl>; <bibl><ptr target="#Malkin-Blok2024"/>, <citedRange>160 n. 28</citedRange></bibl>; <bibl><ptr target="#DomínguezMonedero2026"/>, <citedRange>94</citedRange> (on <foreign xml:lang="grc">παμπασία</foreign>)</bibl>; <bibl><ptr target="#Lipka2026"/>, <citedRange>18 n.34</citedRange></bibl>; <bibl><ptr target="#Frank2026"/>, <citedRange>XXX</citedRange></bibl>.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div type="edition" xml:space="preserve" xml:lang="grc">
            <div type="textpart" subtype="face" n="A">
                <ab>
                    <lb n="1"/>θεός⸱ τύχα ἀγαθά⸱
                    <lb n="2"/>περὶ πανπασίας καὶ περὶ Ϝοικσιος 
                    <lb n="3"/>ἰς Κρ<supplied reason="omitted">ό</supplied>τνα  βέλτιων καὶ ἄμεινο<supplied reason="omitted">ν</supplied>
                    <lb n="4"/>αὐτι καὶ γενε
<lb n="5" break="no"/>ᾶι <pc type="wordDivider">:</pc> καὶ γυναι
<lb n="6" break="no"/>κί;
                </ab>
            </div>
            <div type="textpart" subtype="face" n="B">
        <ab>
      <lb n="1"/>ἐν Κρότνι
        </ab>
        </div>
        </div>
        <div type="apparatus" xml:space="preserve">
            <app loc="l. 3">
                <rdg resp="#Vokotopoulou1992"> <supplied reason="omitted">ε</supplied>ἰς</rdg>
                <rdg resp="#IDodoneLhôte"> ἰς</rdg> <note> and the subsequent editors.</note>
            </app>
                <app loc="l. 3">
                    <rdg><foreign xml:lang="grc">ΚΡΤΟΝΑ</foreign></rdg> <note>tablet, correcting the previously engraved <foreign xml:lang="grc">ΚΤΤΟΝΑ</foreign>, according to the editors of <ptr target="#IDodoneDVC"/>.</note>
                </app>
            <app loc="l. 3">
                <rdg resp="#SEG #Eidinow2007">βέλτιον</rdg>
            </app>
            <app loc="l. 3"> <rdg><foreign xml:lang="grc">ΑΜΕΙΝΟ</foreign></rdg> <note>tablet</note> <rdg resp="#Vokotopoulou1992">ἄμεινον </rdg>
             </app>
        </div>    
        <div type="translation" xml:space="preserve" xml:lang="en">
            <p>God. Good Fortune. About property and migration to Kroton, is it better and more advantageous for him, for his descendance and for his wife?</p>
<p>In Kroton. </p>
        </div>
        <div type="translation" xml:space="preserve" xml:lang="es">
            <p>Dios. Buena Fortuna. Sobre el conjunto de las propiedades y la migración a Crotón, ¿es mejor y más ventajoso para él, para su descendencia y para su mujer?</p>
<p>En Crotón.</p>
        </div>
        <div type="commentary" xml:space="preserve" xml:lang="en">  
            <p>According to Lhôte, this is an Epirote consulting about moving to Kroton (<foreign xml:lang="fr">Crotón es colonia aquea; “des similitudes étroites avec le nº 116, et la forme <foreign xml:lang="grc">ἰς</foreign>, permettent de supposer que le consultant es un Épirote qui envisage d’émigrer à Crotone, aunque antes ha dicho que el alfabeto, y en concreto la forma de la gamma, “pourrait être achéenne, ce qui pourrait amener à penser que le consultant es originaire d’une autre colonie achéenne d’Italie du Sud”).</foreign> Contra Johnston. Alphabet (<bibl><ptr target="#Vokotopoulou1992"/>, <citedRange>83</citedRange></bibl> = <foreign xml:lang="fr">“l’alphabet peut être de la Grande Grèce, mais pas exclusivement de cette région”</foreign>). </p>
                <p>The name of the same city is reconstructed on the fragmentary tablet <bibl><ptr target="#IDodoneDVC"/> <citedRange>319</citedRange></bibl> (<foreign xml:lang="grc"><gap reason="lost" extent="unknown" unit="character"/><supplied reason="lost">Κ</supplied>ρότονι</foreign>), which Lhôte (<bibl><ptr target="#CIOD"/></bibl>) attributes to the same hand and interpretes as an earlier version of the present enquiry, although this connection remains conjectural. 
</p>
